    "OWNED reports one aggregate runtime rate per repeat; competitor rows retain 12 per-prompt rates and use their native/server decode timing.",
    "llama.cpp timings came from /completion timings.predicted_per_second; one-token EOS rows expose a 1000000 tok/s sentinel in raw samples, retained but not used as a claim.",
    "vLLM and SGLang rates use client arrival timestamps between streamed token chunks, excluding the first chunk; EOS-short outputs therefore have null/short samples.",
    "W is averaged nvidia-smi power.draw sampled every 500 ms over the timed cell. OWNED W/VRAM are representative telemetry reruns per model/dtype; cold load is in owned stderr and is not repeated in every raw object.",
    "vLLM and SGLang reserved roughly 18.4-18.8 GiB despite small weights; this is resting allocation, not weight size.",
    "The LFM2.5-230M and -350M owned loader cells were attempted exactly as shipped and failed before timing because rope_theta is absent; no config hack was applied."
